        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1002">

                <pb facs="0936" n="924" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg924"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.6354/127: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-07-24T20:00:00-04:00">July 24, 1939—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>581. Your 1014, July 18, 11 a.m. The Department understands that the Chairman of
                    the International Tin Committee has informed Todd and the American consumers
                    that an extra meeting to reconsider the third quarter quota will not be
                    possible. The Department is of the opinion that a critical situation in tin
                    supplies and prices may develop before the September 24 meeting and that in any
                    event that date is very late for a consideration of the fourth quarter
                    quota.</p>
                <p>You are authorized therefore within your discretion to suggest advancement of the
                    date of the scheduled meeting to early in September, so that the Committee may
                    be in a position at the earliest possible moment to take the necessary steps
                    should the fears of consumers prove to be justified.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
